<!--Post: 5971--><!--Time: 1107470751-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5971"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tucker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tucker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 2:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->KAKE has just recieved a postcard from BTK.  I have no details on the card, but just heard that they did indeed receieve, what can be called, a 9th communication from BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5971-->
<!--Post: 5984--><!--Time: 1107472906-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5984"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 3:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The postcard bore the return address: <BR>HAPP KAKEMANN <BR> <BR>and the address of the KAKE Studio. <BR> <BR>Go wordsleuths - go! <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5984-->
<!--Post: 5985--><!--Time: 1107473087-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5985"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 3:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->They are not releasing part of what the postcard said - but in one part, BTK offers his condolences to Susan Peters and Jeff for their colds.   <BR> <BR>The rest was blacked out.  So the WPD could pretend they&#39;re &#34;on the job&#34;.   <BR> <BR>Who wonders if it is not the affirmation of the little post BeeTeeKay left earlier today here? <BR> <BR>Did he reveal a killing in 1993? <BR> <BR>Who could it be if it is linked?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5985-->
<!--Post: 5987--><!--Time: 1107474007-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5987"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 3:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippy, I just read your post to BTK where you mention WPD has just swabbed Larry Hatteberg for DNA.  Where&#39;d you get that info? <BR> <BR>I Googled him, and the WPD might not be so crazy.  LH did start out as a photojournalist.  He&#39;s the right age range. He&#39;s lived in Wichita for a long time.  He trained as a teacher and his wife&#39;s a teacher, and they have 2 grown kids, and BTK is apparently comfortable dealing with kids.... <BR> <BR>Who are Susan Peters and Jeff?  KAKE anchors?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5987-->
<!--Post: 5988--><!--Time: 1107474466-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5988"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 3:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It was on the 5pm newscast.  Larry mentioned it - said the WPD had gotten a call about him - so he was swabbed. <BR> <BR>That doesn&#39;t look too good.  If they don&#39;t have some evidence that would rule out guys like Larry - then they don&#39;t have any evidence of any significance. <BR> <BR>Susan and Jeff are anchors.  Susan used to be with KWCH  - then moved away, CA, I think, about 15 years ago, then returned to Wichita and took up with KAKE. <BR> <BR>Larry is quite high-profile, does books and segments called &#34;Hatteburg&#39;s People&#34;.  He a real down-to-earth farm sort.  Been with KAKE forever, it seems. <BR> <BR>He&#39;s kind of little and wimpy however.  I doubt he could overpower his mother, much less a family of four trained in Judo.   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5988-->
<!--Post: 5989--><!--Time: 1107474470-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5989"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 3:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is som info on Susan Peters <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/station/bios/news/12121.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/station/bios/news/12121.html</a> <BR> <BR>And Jeff Herndon &#40;I guess its him&#41; <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/station/bios/news/12266.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/station/bios/news/12266.html</a> <BR> <BR>What is interesting IMO is HOW BTK knows that they have a cold??? if they in fact HAS a cold.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5989-->
<!--Post: 5991--><!--Time: 1107475022-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5991"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 3:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->They DID have colds last week, they mentioned they had the &#34;crud&#34; in a newscast.  He must have been watching. <BR> <BR>BTW - the return address name &#34;kakeman&#34; is &#40;may be&#41; a play on what used to be a very popular children&#39;s hour they had on KAKE called KAKEman.  Little puppet show.  I didn&#39;t see it - but I&#39;ve heard about it and they recently did some sort of anniversary commemorating it.  Called it the &#34;longest running&#34; kids show on KAKE or something like that.   <BR> <BR>Why KAKE?  They&#39;re not all that great.  There are two other stations - and one of them is higher rated - KWCH.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5991-->
<!--Post: 5993--><!--Time: 1107475743-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5993"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 4:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here  is a link to a video newsreport on the latest postcard: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/1227847.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/1227847.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5993-->
<!--Post: 6002--><!--Time: 1107477533-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6002"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Purple<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Purple<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 4:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kakeman was a puppet that was on Henry Harvey&#39;s Santa Show on Kake.  It was eventually switched to another network and he became Toyboy.  Henry Harvey died a few years ago.  He did kids shows in the Wichita area.  One was reading the Sunday funnies on Sunday morning.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6002-->
<!--Post: 6014--><!--Time: 1107479552-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6014"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Researcher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Researcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 5:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well from the photo of the latest postcard I see that BTK corrected the position of the : this time that I commented on.  See my post here re: The Postcard 01/31/05. <BR> <BR>Maybe a coincidence.  Maybe he is reading this board carefully.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6014-->
<!--Post: 6032--><!--Time: 1107485414-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6032"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 6:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My post was deleeted so now I´m posting it again moderated. <BR> <BR>There is a person with the last name HAPP &#40; Happ Kakemann the return adress ofthe latest postcard&#41; living aprox. 2 miles from the#8 BTK drop in Valley center.  <BR> <BR>The same person in 1997 had an email adress related to Wichita.Boeing.Com  <BR> <BR>I´m NOT sugesting that this person is related to BTK case at all, but BTK mighthave used this persons name for som reson unknown to me, OR I´m just way off here? <BR>  <BR>   <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6032-->
<!--Post: 6064--><!--Time: 1107516092-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6064"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bakerwood<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bakerwood<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 3:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Happ is one of the sons in Death Of A Salesman. He was a football hero/BMOC but has lived a life as a failure in his father&#39;s eyes. Which, that and $.99 will get you a cup of coffee. <BR>Far more likely that this refers to the Puppet character who appeared on KAKE.   <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6064-->
<!--Post: 6070--><!--Time: 1107524002-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6070"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 5:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found this post on the net. It is from a former paramedic who calls himself Cranky. <BR>It is about the puppet called &#34;Cakeman&#34; <BR> <BR><a href="http://66.102.9.104/search?q=cache:9GwQAmF4NjQJ:www.crankychick.net/blog/weblog/archives/000328.html%2B%22Henry%2BHarvey%22%2B%2Bpuppet&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=lang_en" target=_top>http://66.102.9.104/search?q=cache:9GwQAmF4NjQJ:ww w.crankychick.net/blog/weblog/archives/000328.html &#43;%22Henry&#43;Harvey%22&#43;%2Bpuppet&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=lang_en</a> <BR> <BR>He &#40;Henry Harvey, added by me&#41; also had a pretty fiery little side kick - a hand puppet worked by someone behind the set, first named &#34;Cakeman&#34;, complete with bakers outfit, and then years later, changed to &#34;Toy Boy&#34; with his elf hat and tassle, and exuberant, high pitched little voice. He would help Santa count down the days till Christmas, mark it on a chalk board, and then twirl his little head around in a circle such that his tassle spun violently, as he exclaimed, &#34;Oh, boy, Santee! We&#39;ll go ZOOMING and ZOOMING around the big wide world delivering presents to all the boys and girls!&#34; He was an excitable little fella. The banter between he and Santa was often exceptionally funny, and I&#39;m grinning from ear to ear just thinking about it now. <BR> <BR>Here is the program mentioned at kansas.com : <BR> <BR><a href="http://66.102.9.104/search?q=cache:P9aL3ODKN7AJ:www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/entertainment/10449710.htm%2B%22Henry%2BHarvey%2B%22%2B%2Bwichita&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=lang_en" target=_top>http://66.102.9.104/search?q=cache:P9aL3ODKN7AJ:ww w.kansas.com/mld/kansas/entertainment/10449710.htm &#43;%22Henry&#43;Harvey&#43;%22&#43;%2Bwichita&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=lang_en</a> <BR> <BR>Monday <BR> <BR>5:30 p.m. &#40;Channel 5&#41; &#34;Santa&#39;s Workshop&#34; &#40;children&#41;. Locally made daily countdown to Christmas by Santa &#40;Henry Harvey&#41; with sidekicks ToyBoy and Montague Moose. This is the 1983 season of the series that ran for three generations. <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6070-->
<!--Post: 6124--><!--Time: 1107540043-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6124"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 10:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->An interesting and very wide array of products from Happ Controls including, surveillance equipment.  <BR> <BR>Just wondering if KAKE has any of Happ Controls equipment or knows of any involved with the BTK investigation. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.happcontrols.com/" target=_top>www.happcontrols.com/</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6124-->
